Lumentum Holdings Inc. (LITE) slashed its fiscal second-quarter revenue and earnings outlook after optical equipment maker said it received a request from "one of its largest" customers to "materially reduce shipments" for previously placed orders. The stock was halted for news until 8:30 a.m. Eastern. The company cut his guidance range for adjusted earnings per share to $1.15 to $1.34 from $1.60 to $1.75, compared with the FactSet consensus of $1.67, and for revenue to $335 million to $355 million from $405 million to $430 million, compared with expectations of $420.5 million. In Lumentum's 10-K annual report for the fiscal year ended June 30, the company said its largest customers in terms of percent of revenue were Apple Inc. (AAPL) at 30%, Huawei at 11% and Ciena Corp. (CIEN) at 11%. Lumentum's stock, which was inactive prior to the halt, has lost 4.5% over the past three months while the S&P 500 has slipped 1.8%.
-Tomi Kilgore;
